{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"procedural mesh growth algorithms procedural mesh growth algorithms","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms.md","fileName":"Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Procedural Mesh Editing with bmesh]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Procedural Mesh Editing with bmesh","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"procedural mesh growth algorithms procedural mesh growth algorithms","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms.md","fileName":"Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms","heading":"Procedural Mesh Growth Algorithms","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A mesh-growth algorithm repeatedly chooses a region, selects its components, and extrudes or transforms them according to a rule. Random choices can produce organic variation, while deterministic rules can construct repeatable architectural, mathematical, or scientific forms.\n\nThe geometry is produced by the procedure rather than stored as a finished asset. Parameters such as bounds, direction probabilities, step size, and iteration limits define a family of models. Reliable growth depends on selection by geometry and careful mode management because every iteration changes the topology on which the next decision operates.","tag